nodecode-prediction-markets is a rewrite of predictionmarketspicks's predictionmarketspicks/mcp:

  https://github.com/predictionmarketspicks/mcp
  commit d1abeb5562f54f0f6950d117669dce290fe1a1b6
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 PredictionMarketsPicks (LICENSE)

The plugin is configuration only: mcp.json (a hosted MCP server over Streamable
HTTP) and the prediction-markets skill. The calculator half of that server is
also shipped by the same repository as a self-contained offline build
(`--local`), and that build is what this cell rewrites in Common Lisp:

  calc.lisp        src/lib/formulas.js, src/lib/combo-price.js and the
                   arithmetic of src/tools.js: the EV edge, Kelly sizing,
                   Bayesian updating, probability / American / decimal
                   conversion, the base-rate gap and the combo fair-value
                   band, with the original's rounding and thresholds.
  cell.lisp        the six tool schemas of src/tools.js as boundary
                   contracts, the twelve curated base rates of
                   src/lib/base-rates.js as data, and the skill's rules as
                   (help :prediction-markets).

Left out, and why: the other 34 tools on the hosted endpoint (live Kalshi and
Polymarket boards, Fed odds, perps, the NFL model) answer live market data
from predictionmarketspicks.com and are not in this repository's own source, so
a rewrite of them would be a client of that server rather than a port of this
code; point the mcp cell at https://predictionmarketspicks.com/api/mcp/mcp for
them. Also left out: the branded footer each result carried (a UTM backlink to
the site's tool page and a Kalshi signup referral), and the JSON `structured`
mirror of every answer, which is text here.
